        - A middle ground would be an option to the REPL that lets you log to a file.
          This would capture all input/output, but not like script, which captures all
          keystrokes; you'd just want it to capture the finished line that's submitted
          to the REPL.  Of course, for critical stuff, you could use script as needed.
          I'm leaning towards the REPL log, as it should be straightforward to
          implement, give you that critical history when needed, and doesn't require
          lots of code.
